  "id": "biomedical-informatics",
  "term": "biomedical informatics",
  "definition": "Biomedical informatics is a healthcare research area that uses large electronic health record data together with statistical and machine-learning methods to make predictions that can improve care. In this context, it includes tasks such as filling in missing data, forecasting a known patient’s future condition, and applying patterns learned from past patients to new patients.",
